       }
      ],
      "text": "**At the latest reading I can see, KL’s API was 170—“unhealthy,” but below the school-closure threshold of 200.** The ministry says outdoor school activities should stop above 100, and parents may keep children home if worried about their health, as long as they notify the school. ([jerebu.com](https://www.jerebu.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\nSo: **they don’t automatically need to skip, but keeping them home is reasonable**—especially if they have asthma or other breathing problems, are already feeling unwell, or would spend much time outdoors getting to school. If they go, check with the school about indoor activities and avoid outdoor exertion. Readings can change, so check the DOE’s live API and the school’s updates before deciding.",
